# Shell scripts run on macOS and reach it verbatim through a checkout, so a CRLF
# working tree breaks them at the shebang: `/bin/zsh` is not a file that
# exists, and the error blames the interpreter rather than the line ending.
# Observed exactly that way after a Python rewrite of the deploy scripts on
# Windows, back when they were shipped by scp -- which CLAUDE.md §1 now forbids,
# though the hazard is identical for a script git checks out.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.plist text eol=lf
